  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "text": "Mara had tied white ribbons to the six orchard rows that morning. Each ribbon marked fruit promised to a different kitchen, including the kitchen where Ivo cooked for the school. Now the weather bell was ringing for an overnight frost. There were blankets in the shed, but the branches were too low to drape carelessly. “The bees ruined the early blossoms,” Mara said, repeating the explanation she had heard all week. “Perhaps covering these will keep them out.” Ivo looked at the darkening sky. They had a few hours, and no spare spring.",
      "evidence": [
        "e001"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "valley.frost",
        "mara.belief",
        "rows.total"
      ],
      "id": "night0.1",
      "drama": "night0"
    },
    {
      "text": "At the end of the first row, Mara bent over the damaged branch they had kept for comparison. The unopened buds were black inside; even flowers under a fine mesh bag had the same injury. A dated frost marker beside the branch matched the night of the damage. Bees had never entered that bag. “Cold,” she said at last. “We have been blaming the thing that brings us fruit.” The discovery did not mend a single blossom. It did change what she meant to shut out tonight.",
      "evidence": [
        "e002"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "trial.cause",
        "mara.observed_cause",
        "mara.belief"
      ],
      "id": "night1.1",
      "drama": "night1"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ivo found his father's field notebook inside the jammed glass cabinet beside the orchard bench. Mara could see the leather cover but could not reach the pages. They tried lifting the warped door; the frame held. “There was a drawing about frost,” Ivo said, unable to remember its details. The notebook stayed behind the glass, carrying instructions neither of them could use. Outside, Mara spread a blanket on the bench and considered what she could test before risking the six rows.",
      "evidence": [
        "e003"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "notebook.accessible",
        "mara.meme.air_gap",
        "mara.meme.anchor_edges"
      ],
      "id": "night2.1",
      "drama": "night2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mara tried the blanket on the comparison branch. It sagged against the flowers, and a loose edge lifted every time the wind crossed the bench. The little cup beneath it cooled as quickly as its uncovered twin. She took the blanket off before its damp weight bent the twig. “That isn't a shelter yet,” she admitted. The failed trial spared the orchard a false promise, but it had consumed the last margin of light. They still had cloth, and still lacked a working way to use it.",
      "evidence": [
        "e004"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "trial.tested",
        "trial.protected",
        "trial.air_gap",
        "trial.anchored",
        "trial.retains_warmth",
        "trial.resistance",
        "valley.trial_cold"
      ],
      "id": "night3.1",
      "drama": "night3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ivo held out his long fork, the one with his initials burned into the handle. It could lift cloth above the branches without tearing it. “Borrow it until morning,” he said. Mara took it carefully; the tool was still his, even while her hands controlled it. Then he rolled up his sleeves. “You raise the roof; I'll carry stones and close the sides.” They would be able to move along the rows together, with neither leaving a half-finished shelter behind.",
      "evidence": [
        "e005"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "fork.owner",
        "fork.user",
        "ivo.willing"
      ],
      "id": "night4.1",
      "drama": "night4"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mara carried the fork between the rows, then stopped. The bench trial had given her no working shelter to repeat. Raising a sheet for a moment did not keep it raised through a windy night. She folded the blankets beside the gate instead of loading the blossoms with wet cloth. Ivo's tool lay across the folded heap, useful and insufficient. Six white ribbons moved freely above six exposed rows as the first frost silvered the latch.",
      "evidence": [
        "e006"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "rows.protected"
      ],
      "id": "night5.1",
      "drama": "night5"
    },
    {
      "text": "At sunrise Mara returned to the ribbons. Every exposed row held black-centered flowers. No living blossoms remained among the six marked rows. She counted carefully: no rows had surviving blossoms. There was no quarrel left to have with the bees. Cold had done this, and the night's work had determined how much of it the orchard could withstand.",
      "evidence": [
        "e007"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "rows.surviving",
        "valley.outcome",
        "valley.night_cold",
        "rows.resistance"
      ],
      "id": "night6.1",
      "drama": "night6"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mara wiped the fork's handle and returned it to Ivo. His initials emerged from beneath the soil. She gathered all six white ribbons and laid them beside the shut notebook. Beyond the bench, a bee landed on an unmarked weed in bloom. Mara left it undisturbed.",
      "evidence": [
        "e008"
      ],
      "reveals": [
        "fork.user",
        "fork.returned",
        "fork.owner"
      ],
      "id": "night7.1",
      "drama": "night7"
    }
  ],
  "qa": [
    {
      "question": "What threatened the promised orchard fruit?",
      "answer": "An overnight frost threatened the blossoms on six marked rows. Mara wanted to preserve the fruit already promised to the community kitchens.",
